@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Configured model (never returns the API key)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/dev/model

### Complete a conversation
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/dev/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"messages": [
		{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one short sentence."}
	]
}

### Exceed the context budget before contacting the provider (match context_tokens from /model)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/dev/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"messages": [
		{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello."}
	],
	"max_output_tokens": 8192
}

### Bad provider key (restart the API with a deliberately invalid LLM_API_KEY first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/dev/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"messages": [
		{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello."}
	]
}

### Provider unavailable (restart the API with LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1/v1 first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/dev/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"messages": [
		{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello."}
	]
}

### Extract a job's technical skill graph (requires API_DEV_ROUTES=true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/dev/extract-skills
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"job_title": "Junior React Developer",
	"job_description": "Build accessible user interfaces with React and TypeScript."
}

